      "sort": 600,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "flags": {},
      "type": "weapon",
      "system": {
        "type": {
          "value": "natural",
          "baseItem": ""
        },
        "description": {
          "value": "<p><em>Melee Weapon Attack:</em> +8, reach 5 ft. <em>Hit:</em> 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, and the stonemaw has no more than three Medium or Small creatures swallowed, then the target is subjected to the following effect. <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 16 Strength. <em>Failure:</em> The target is swallowed.</p><p>A swallowed target is Blinded and Restrained, it has Total Cover against attacks and other effects outside the stonemaw, and it takes 15 (6d4) Acid damage at the start of each of the stonemaw's turns. If the stonemaw takes 20 damage or more on a single turn from sources inside it, it must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, each of which falls Prone in a space within 10 feet of the stonemaw. If the stonemaw dies, any swallowed creature is no longer Restrained by it and can escape from the corpse using 15 feet of movement, exiting Prone.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
